        "answer": {
          "short": "501.\n\nAdding 3 gives the lowest common multiple of 7, 8 and 9.",
          "worked": "Each remainder is 3 less than its divisor, so adding 3 to the required number gives a common multiple of 7, 8 and 9.\n\nThe first common multiple of 7 and 8 is 56. Its multiples are $56,112,168,224,280,336,392,448,504,\\ldots$. The first divisible by 9 is 504, so this is the lowest common multiple of all three numbers.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}n&=504-3\\\\n&=501\\end{align*}$$\nCheck: $501=7\\times71+4$, $501=8\\times62+5$ and $501=9\\times55+6$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 55
      },
